<p>I also convolve the selfie with finite difference filters. D<sub>x</sub> measures changes across columns, so vertical boundaries appear strongly. D<sub>y</sub> measures changes across rows, so horizontal boundaries appear strongly. In the derivative displays, gray is zero, white is positive, and black is negative.</p>
<pre><code># Define finite-difference filters
