<section id="part-2-3"><h3>Part 2.3: Gaussian and Laplacian Stacks</h3>
<p>I build six Gaussian levels for each fruit. Level 0 is the original image. To create each next level, I blur the previous one with σ = 2, 4, 8, 16, and 32 in order. These are successive blur widths, so each level includes the smoothing from earlier levels. Every level keeps the original 300 × 300 dimensions.</p>
<p>This uses the scale separation described in Section 2 of <a href="https://www.cs.princeton.edu/courses/archive/fall05/cos429/papers/burt_adelson.pdf">Burt and Adelson’s A Multiresolution Spline With Application to Image Mosaics</a>. Their pyramids reduce image dimensions between levels. My stacks retain the full dimensions, as the project requires.</p>
