<section id="reflection"><h2>What I learned</h2>
<p>The most important thing I learned was the difference between Gaussian and Laplacian stacks. A Gaussian level contains the image after repeated blurring. A Laplacian level contains the detail lost between two Gaussian levels. Keeping the final blurred image lets me add the Laplacian levels back together to reconstruct the original. In the blends, I can control how each level crosses the mask boundary.</p>
